{
  "esm": "1.0.0",
  "metadata": {
    "name": "integral_lev_nodes_cumulative_to_top",
    "description": "Cumulative integral from each INTERFACE to the MODEL TOP: lowers integral(f, var: lev, lower: lev_nodes, upper: b) -- the lower bound literally the interface axis name -- to the interface field G[kn] = sum_{j>=kn} f[j] dz[j] over kn in lev_nodes (shape [lev_nodes]): G[NLEV+1] = 0 at the top and G[1] the whole-column integral at the surface. Whole layers only, exact telescoping with face_flux_D_lev_supplied_faces (D(G, wrt: lev) = -f). This is the optical depth from the top of the atmosphere down to each interface, the quantity a two-stream or Beer-Lambert shortwave scheme (e.g. WRF's Dudhia scheme) needs at the level interfaces where it evaluates fluxes. The integrand `f` must be a bare layer-shaped (lev) field of THIS grid (where {f: {shape: [lev]}}, esm-spec 9.6.1); bind a compound integrand to a declared [lev] observed first. The measure is the consumer's free-name layer-thickness observed `dz` (grids/column_nonuniform_1d/grid.esm) -- rebind it at the import edge (esm-spec 9.7.7) to integrate against another monotone layer measure such as dp/g. The integral node's `var` names the axis (`lev`); esm-spec 4.2 leaves the bounds measure-free, so the bounds carry no numeric weight here: they select the FORM of the sum (whole column / cumulative from the surface / cumulative from the top / to layer centres / to interfaces) and are otherwise documentation. Because the layer values are midpoint samples, every form is the composite midpoint rule and is second-order accurate on a smoothly stretched column.",
    "license": "MIT",
    "tags": [
      "esd:rule",
      "family:finite_volume",
      "grid:column_nonuniform_1d",
      "op:integral",
      "order:2",
      "stencil_width:1",
      "bc:none",
      "spec:9.6.8",
      "axes:lev_nodes"
    ],
    "references": [
      {
        "citation": "LeVeque, R. J. (2007). Finite Difference Methods for Ordinary and Partial Differential Equations. SIAM. Section 2.13 (nonuniform grids)."
      },
      {
        "citation": "Davis, P. J. and Rabinowitz, P. (1984). Methods of Numerical Integration, 2nd ed. Academic Press. Section 2.1 (the midpoint rule and its error)."
      }
    ]
  },
  "expression_template_imports": [
    {
      "ref": "../grid.esm"
    }
  ],
  "expression_templates": {
    "integral_lev_nodes_cumulative_to_top": {
      "params": [
        "f",
        "b"
      ],
      "priority": 10,
      "match": {
        "op": "integral",
        "args": [
          "f"
        ],
        "var": "lev",
        "lower": "lev_nodes",
        "upper": "b"
      },
      "where": {
        "f": {
          "shape": [
            "lev"
          ]
        }
      },
      "body": {
        "op": "aggregate",
        "output_idx": [
          "kn"
        ],
        "reduce": "+",
        "args": [
          "f"
        ],
        "ranges": {
          "kn": {
            "from": "lev_nodes"
          },
          "j": {
            "from": "lev"
          }
        },
        "filter": {
          "op": ">=",
          "args": [
            "j",
            "kn"
          ]
        },
        "expr": {
          "op": "*",
          "args": [
            {
              "op": "index",
              "args": [
                "f",
                "j"
              ]
            },
            {
              "op": "index",
              "args": [
                "dz",
                "j"
              ]
            }
          ]
        }
      }
    }
  }
}
